+whereas the probability that two randomly chosen residents on a non-HOA block are of dif-
+ferent races is 20 percent. As shown in Table 4, the 0.06 diﬀerence is statistically signiﬁcant
+even if we allow errors to be correlated across blocks within the same county. 21 However,
