+a vector of house- and transaction-speciﬁc characteristics; gj is a vector of geographic area
+(block group) ﬁxed eﬀects; ηt is a vector of month-by-year ﬁxed eﬀects; and ϵijt is the error
+term.
+In equation (1), the main coeﬃcient of interest, β1, is identiﬁed oﬀ variation in HOA
+status across observationally equivalent homes sold at a similar point in time within a small
+geographic area. Our use of block group ﬁxed eﬀects is motivated by a desire to restrict com-
+parisons to nearby homes that not only share similar observable and unobservable property
+characteristics, but also are subject to the same local government taxes and regulations and
+have access to the same set of (non-HOA) public goods and services. One concern, however,
